I've been working on a better approach, and realized the cleanest way to fix the fade issue is to use a wrapper div.  The outer div will manage the opacity, and the inner will handle the background. This will prevent conflicts between the gradient animation and the fade-in. I'm going to check the `App.tsx` implementation to see how to implement this.


